  "releaseNotes": "1.0.1 — re-release of 1.0.0 packaged end-to-end by the standard release workflow so the .nupkg bytes published to nuget.org match the SLSA-style build-provenance attestation and verify cleanly against a clean-room Linux rebuild via .github/workflows/reproducibility.yml. No library code change since 1.0.0 — the library, the .pqfe v2 format, the public API surface, and the runtime dependencies are identical. Adds .gitattributes (force LF repo-wide so cross-OS rebuilds match the Linux-published bytes) and a .psmdcp exclusion in the reproducibility script (NuGet's per-pack GUID metadata is never reproducible by design). 1.0.0's published nupkg was hand-recovered on Windows during the release-key rotation; 1.0.1 closes that supply-chain loop. EnablePackageValidation against the 1.0.0 baseline. See CHANGELOG.md.",
